{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dear Marie,\n\nI was at the theater this evening and saw Romeo and Juliet. The English company performed. Kemble was Romeo. There were two things that struck me as deviating from the play. First: In the first scene, Romeo sat next to Juliet before he spoke. Second: Mercutio joked with the Nurse when she interrupted them. But what surprised me most was the ending. Juliet woke up while Romeo was still alive, after he had taken the poison. He did not die before she opened her eyes, as we know it. It was a strange sight.\n\nThe air in Paris is pleasant today, and I felt well. I am writing this to you only because I could not say it immediately in Berlin.\n\nYour G. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795221213,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":159,"prompt_tokens":251,"total_tokens":410,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-g5tZAK5KNMgvq2x23tvdoOUtr2kpK43M","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":251,"prompt_ms":404.97,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.6134262948207172,"prompt_per_second":619.7989974566017,"predicted_n":159,"predicted_ms":3692.074,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.36755696202532,"predicted_per_second":42.79437519399666}}